"""Append actual recovery evidence; unequal-budget pilot, not frontier."""
import json,sys
from pathlib import Path
from docx import Document
from docx.oxml import OxmlElement
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'experiments'));import paper50 as P
p=ROOT/'paper/MEGA27-23b-50p.docx';d=Document(p);title='Joint whole-file recovery: a clean gate and a retained silent-wrong result'
assert not any(x.text==title for x in d.paragraphs)
j=json.loads((ROOT/'results/block_joint_file_audit.json').read_text())
P.h1(d,title)
P.para(d,'The distance-five detector now enters an audit-local complete-file wrapper alongside the low-byte and full Fletcher detectors. We do not replace the production codec or claim matched-budget superiority. All three candidates use the same twelve-trit length header, six-trit-per-byte representation, global twelve-trit Fletcher check, scrambling, 32-trit payload blocks and one outer componentwise mod-three parity block. They differ in local check length: six, twelve or sixteen trits. Each file is represented by one continuous seeded-block strand, repeated either once or three times. The geometry does not model a segmented oligo pool or physical molecular reads.')
P.para(d,'The wrapper decodes a per-position plurality sequence, tries individual copies if a block fails its local check, and repairs a single missing payload block when outer parity passes. The audit fixes ties in A,C,G,T order. Production uses a set-based tie order that depends on the Python hash seed, so this wrapper is not identical to the production decoder. It also explicitly rejects malformed lengths, out-of-range headers and byte values above 255. Those checks help separate framing errors from recovery but do not eliminate checksum collisions. Copy fallback selects the first passing payload and does not reconcile disagreement among multiple passing candidates.')
P.h2(d,'Message identities, repeated noise and the clean gate')
P.para(d,'The fixed generator seed 930481 creates sixteen 128-byte and four 2,048-byte messages. Each detector/copy condition receives those same twenty identities and three noise realizations per identity. Strict independent substitutions use rates 0, .005, .01, .02 and .03, with each changed letter drawn from exactly the three alternatives to its original base. The channel operates on every encoded base, including local and global checks, headers and outer parity. Noise seeds are reproducible, but unequal lengths consume the generator differently: matching seeds is not matching corrupted positions. The experiment totals 1,800 file trials across six detector/copy configurations and five rates.')
P.para(d,'All six configurations recover all sixty clean trials exactly. The sixty trials represent twenty distinct files with three identical zero-noise repetitions, not sixty independent clean files. Clean success is a necessary gate that earlier invalid codec ports did not always pass, but it does not establish a noisy advantage. A comparison that fails this gate should stop before interpreting its error curves. Here the gate passes, allowing the noisy failures and costs to be reported without hiding them behind a detector-only success.')
P.table(d,'Three-copy complete-file counts. Each cell is exact success / loud failure / silent wrong among 60 repeated-measure trials.',['Strict p','Low-byte 38 nt','Full Fletcher 44 nt','Distance-five 48 nt'],[['0','60 / 0 / 0','60 / 0 / 0','60 / 0 / 0'],['.005','59 / 1 / 0','59 / 1 / 0','60 / 0 / 0'],['.01','45 / 15 / 0','54 / 6 / 0','54 / 6 / 0'],['.02','34 / 26 / 0','40 / 20 / 0','41 / 19 / 0'],['.03','17 / 41 / 2','24 / 36 / 0','23 / 37 / 0']])
P.para(d,'At one copy, the low-byte candidate recovers one of sixty trials at p=.005; the other fifty-nine fail loudly. Full Fletcher and distance-five both fail loudly in all sixty trials at that rate. At .01, .02 and .03 every one-copy candidate trial fails loudly. A detector does not create redundancy that recovers many erased blocks: one outer parity block cannot repair multiple missing blocks. Stronger detection can remove wrong acceptance but cannot make the one-copy architecture useful in this library. These failures remain part of the result rather than being omitted from the plot or averaged into the three-copy condition.')
P.h2(d,'A production-reproducible silent wrong counterexample')
P.para(d,'The fixed-order low-byte audit decoder produces two silent wrong outputs at p=.03 with three copies: 128-byte messages 3 and 4, both at noise replicate 1. It returns bytes without an exception, but the bytes differ from the expected file. The saved negative-case JSON retains exact noisy strands, expected bytes, returned bytes and production replay. Through the unmodified production decode_message_v2 under PYTHONHASHSEED=0, message 3 reproduces the same wrong result while message 4 decodes correctly. A subprocess regression fixes that hash seed and requires the message-3 production output to differ from the expected file. This is an existence counterexample to never-silent-corruption, not a claim that both audit cases fail under every production tie order.')
P.para(d,'The README guarantee is withdrawn. A global Fletcher check can accept a wrong body if its checksum collides; a passing local low-byte check and first-passing-copy policy do not prevent that route. The present experiment establishes the saved counterexample and does not assign all causal changes to a single local mechanism. A deeper trace of selected block candidates, parity repair and global-check collision would be needed to attribute the complete failure chain. Randomness in a production tie policy is also not a safety guarantee. Deterministic comparison should state the policy, while an implementation used outside this audit should reject or deliberately resolve conflicting validated candidates.')
P.para(d,'Neither full Fletcher nor distance-five produces a silent wrong output in these 600 noisy/clean trials per detector across copy conditions, but absence in a finite library is not a whole-file theorem. The distance-five proposition covers at most two substitutions in an aligned isolated block. A file channel can place more substitutions in a block, and plurality/fallback can create a candidate with a different effective error pattern. The global check remains Fletcher for every wrapper. The stronger candidate therefore receives no universal whole-file integrity guarantee from the local distance proof.')
P.h2(d,'Finite-size geometry, constraints and the copy budget')
P.table(d,'Charged three-copy geometry. Headers, padding, one outer parity block and local checks included; primers/indexes/physical molecules excluded.',['Bytes','Detector','Strand nt','Total nt','Bits / nt'],[[128,'Low-byte',988,2964,'.345479'],[128,'Full Fletcher',1144,3432,'.298368'],[128,'Distance-five',1248,3744,'.273504'],[2048,'Low-byte',14668,44004,'.372330'],[2048,'Full Fletcher',16984,50952,'.321558'],[2048,'Distance-five',18528,55584,'.294761']])
P.para(d,'The candidate exact-recovery counts improve over low-byte detection in several conditions, but full Fletcher and distance-five exchange small leads as noise changes. At p=.01 both recover 54 of 60; at .02 the counts are 40 and 41; at .03 they are 24 and 23. Different budgets, lengths and affected positions prevent a causal superiority inference from these differences. Repeated noise realizations on the same files also forbid treating sixty trials as sixty independent message identities for a simple confidence interval. The saved ledger permits stratification by payload size and message instead of silently mixing these units.')
P.para(d,'All clean full strands in this library have maximum homopolymer run two, not one. Each isolated seeded block excludes equal adjacent bases, but block joins can create equal-letter seams. A whole-strand HP1 constraint therefore fails for these encodings. The ledger records whole-strand GC fraction for every file; the experiment does not screen a common GC window, remove violating files, optimize parity density or report a constraint-matched frontier. Nominal one/three identical software copies are not a physical copy model. These constraints must be matched explicitly before comparing a frontier with a published storage codec or an external port.')
P.h2(d,'What this experiment closes and what it leaves open')
P.para(d,'Run PYTHONHASHSEED=0 python3 experiments/block_joint_file_audit.py. The summary and JSONL ledger retain all 1,800 outcomes, changed-base counts, message and clean-DNA digests, charged geometry, whole-strand homopolymers and GC. Saved wrong-case reads support deterministic audit replay and seeded production replay. Regression tests cover clean files of lengths zero, one, 128 and 2,048 bytes, framing cost, trial digest, clean gates, both audit-local wrong outputs and the unmodified production counterexample. The trial SHA256 is shown on two lines below.')
P.para(d,j['ledger_sha256'][:32]+'\n'+j['ledger_sha256'][32:])
P.para(d,'This is a joint clean/noisy complete-file pilot with an honest unequal-budget comparison. The next required result is a preregistered geometry, copy and constraint matched frontier, not another detector checksum substitution. The production silent-wrong claim is disproved and the negative evidence is retained. Manuscript-wide claim consistency across all four projects, audited full-text body growth, independent scientific validation and the user-supplied verdict gate remain separate open tasks. No paper completion, public communication or submission is inferred from the new PDF pages.')
